Running the recover tool on files generated by a nethack process that
did not crash is not necessarily the same as if it did crash.  When
nethack crashes, that often means that there are problems with the 
internal structures which might be reflected in the saved level files
as well.

> The code works period. Any failures come from somewhere
> other than the nethack code. 

Whenever someone declares that a particular piece of software is 
bug-free, my first thought is that person needs more experience.

Given the complexity and history of Nethack, the recover tool 
is quite reliable, but from personal experience I know that it
isn't perfect.  For someone who has never ascended -- which 
means that getting another character that far may take several
days of play -- backing up the save file to protect against
hardware or software failures is probably wise.


